                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b28cd846-d964-3523-982c-2e544e6c0af7",
                        "entry_id": "9f1dd0c1-89cf-3180-bb19-4ba97536e200",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A confection made from a paste of almonds, sugar and egg white as a binder."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dbea7f5-d20b-355c-a8b5-b535f4c8fb0b",
                        "entry_id": "9f1dd0c1-89cf-3180-bb19-4ba97536e200",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A similar confection made using another nut, such as peanut or hazelnut."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ee21f78-991a-44ff-9628-7027256e46aa",
                                "sense_id": "6dbea7f5-d20b-355c-a8b5-b535f4c8fb0b",
                                "text": "Place the hazelnuts on a baking sheet and grill […] then grind finely […] then add the caster sugar and ground hazelnuts [to egg whites] and mix to a stiff marzipan paste. Sandwich the pecan nuts together in pairs with a little of the hazelnut marzipan."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e64a7942-212b-4bca-8d7a-c2ca45daaa50",
                                "sense_id": "6dbea7f5-d20b-355c-a8b5-b535f4c8fb0b",
                                "text": "Hazelnut marzipan. Hazelnuts are used as an alternative to almonds, ground together in a proportion from 11⁄2 to 2 parts nuts to sugar. Almonds may be mixed in according to taste."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1863a57e-06e2-42cf-8924-607e8a5e7e03",
                                "sense_id": "6dbea7f5-d20b-355c-a8b5-b535f4c8fb0b",
                                "text": "[…] cookie mini pack, watermelon Bubble Yum or, my favorite, de la Rosa, a peanut marzipan round packaged in a cellophane wrapper with a delicate rose printed on it. De la Rosa is a perfect confection. Just crumbly enough, just sweet enough […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "249befb9-ad7e-410c-9f46-3b0fcee71681",
                                "sense_id": "6dbea7f5-d20b-355c-a8b5-b535f4c8fb0b",
                                "text": "To make the filling: In a food processor, blend the peanut butter, powdered sugar, salt, and cayenne together. […] THE FILLING RECIPE IS ALSO awfully close to that of peanut marzipan, which you can make yourself by adding more powdered sugar to create a sturdier, shape-able “dough,” or just look for the de la Rosa brand at your local Latino grocery."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1513c135-8552-3c57-95ff-7db9cba56dde",
                        "entry_id": "9f1dd0c1-89cf-3180-bb19-4ba97536e200",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A piece of such a confection."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c0074e2-67a8-4e8d-b553-c4bdacdd1feb",
                                "sense_id": "1513c135-8552-3c57-95ff-7db9cba56dde",
                                "text": "One afternoon not long afterwards you waited byher bedside as she swam through anesthetic. A box of cherry chocolates and a dozen roses in your lap. Cherry chocolates and chocolate-covered marzipans. Then you drove her home. Chocolate-covered marzipans being her favorite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b599f184-9e39-4713-8f43-d5815559a032",
                                "sense_id": "1513c135-8552-3c57-95ff-7db9cba56dde",
                                "text": "In one hand she held a handkerchief, and in the other she held two cherry-shaped marzipans. Rosalia smiled when she saw the marzipans and took them and the handkerchief from Madre Carmela."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
